// Deliberately a diagnostic, not the capture path: it answers "is the module
// wired right and is the gain trimmer somewhere sane" before any streaming
// work exists to be confused by. Reports DC bias (proves power + the OUT wire),
// per-window peak-to-peak (proves it hears you), and a clip count (proves the
// gain isn't cranked past the rails).
// 10s, not 4: the window has to be easy to HIT. At 4s you had to wait ~1.4s of
// floor measurements, catch a short beep, and talk for exactly 4s - and run
// after run recorded only room tone because the talking landed either side of
// it. Ten seconds makes the timing a non-issue; the per-window profile still
// pinpoints when the sound actually happened.
const int MIC_TEST_MS = 10000;
const int MIC_TEST_HZ = 8000;
const int MIC_WIN_MS  = 200;
